<%- include('partials/header') %>
<h1>What would you use Docker for?</h1>
<p class="lede">Docker packages an application together with everything it needs to run (runtime, libraries, config) into an <strong>image</strong>, and runs copies of that image as isolated processes called <strong>containers</strong>. That is the whole idea. Here is what it buys you in practice.</p>
<% uses.forEach((u) => { %>
  <section class="use <%= u.django ? 'callout' : '' %>">
    <h2><%= u.title %></h2>
    <p><%= u.body %></p>
  </section>
<% }) %>
<p><a class="button primary" href="/wizard">Try it on your own project</a></p>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
